IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `refja-registration`

-- Reciprocal Enforcement of Foreign Judgments Act 1959, ss 2, 2A, 3-7, 11-13 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_reciprocal-enforcement-of-foreign-judgments-act-1959.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

`a final judgment of a recognised court` MEANS Judgment WITH
    `is of a recognised court and of a description specified in a section 3 order` IS TRUE
    `was given after the order came into operation` IS TRUE
    `is final and conclusive between the parties` IS TRUE
    `is interlocutory` IS FALSE
    `an appeal is pending or still possible` IS FALSE
    `was given on appeal from a court that is not recognised` IS FALSE
    `was given or made in another foreign country` IS FALSE
    `enforces a judgment of another foreign country` IS FALSE
    `may be enforced under the Choice of Court Agreements Act 2016` IS FALSE

